# A config that is written on the compile mode's declarations
# (`config/init.lean`): it overrides one field of the shipped
# `Compile.cargoMode`, registers a contribution with a format of its own
# and the commands of one project, and defines a command over
# `Compile.Format.read?` and `Compile.shipped`. What it prints must be
# exactly `expected`. It names no path of the machine, starts no process
# and touches no file.

# The config elaborates and installs: the base config is elaborated on
# holds the compile mode's declarations.
reload
settle

# The command config defined says what its format reads of `at src/x.rs
# line 4`, the file and the line, and the modes of the contributions that
# ship, in the echo area.
run compile-reading
scene
